<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Venkatapati Raya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1586–1614</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Venkata II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Venkatapati Raya, or Venkata II, was emperor of Vijayanagara of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aravidu-dynasty">Aravidu dynasty</a> from 1586 to 1614. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penukonda">Penukonda</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragiri">Chandragiri</a>, he restored a measure of royal authority, repelled attacks by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golconda-fort">Golconda</a> and kept the southern nayakas in nominal obedience. His death without a direct heir led to a succession war that further weakened the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/venkatapati-raya.jpg" alt="Venkatapati Raya" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ravitheja Kumar Reddy C · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VenkatapatiRaya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
